{
 "about": "The Nordschleife from the Touristenfahrten gate to the gantry on the Doettinger Hoehe, clockwise. Each point is [east, north] in kilometres with its height in metres, traced by hand from public maps and elevation profiles: the shape, the order of the corners and the big climbs and drops are right, the exact lines are approximate. The game draws a smooth curve through the points, scales it to the real lap length, then shrinks it so a lap takes minutes, not eight. Crests are the jumps (extra height in game metres and the length of the bump); bank is degrees, negative for a left-hander's banking.",
